              "name": "drawable",
              "type": "RenderNode",
              "optional": false
            }
          ],
          "returnType": "boolean",
          "description": "Offer a drawable whose silhouette is its own alpha, and report whether the field took it. false means this field turns occluders into geometry and the source must describe the same shape as segments instead - which is the answer wherever shadows are built on the CPU, so a source that can only do one of the two still works everywhere. Where it is taken, the drawable is rasterised at its own place in the world each frame. That is what makes an animation, a video or a render target cast a correct shadow without a trace, a cache or a warning, and it is why the offer comes first and the geometry second."
        },
